## Document Operations (TipTap)

### Available Operations

- `create`: Create a new TipTap document
- `list`: List all documents across tables
- `read`: Get document content (TipTap JSON)
- `update`: Update document content

### Document Structure

Documents are stored as field values in table rows. Each document has:

```json
{
  "id": "uuid-string",
  "name": "meeting-notes.tiptap.json",
  "title": "Meeting Notes",
  "tableId": 5,
  "tableName": "Documents",
  "rowId": "row-uuid",
  "fieldId": 12,
  "fieldName": "Content",
  "mimeType": "application/vnd.tiptap+json",
  "version": 1
}
```

### Creating Documents

Create in a **new row** (default):
```
document_crud(method="create",
              table_id=5,
              field_id=12,
              title="New Document")
```

Create in an **existing row** (use `row_id`):
```
document_crud(method="create",
              table_id=5,
              field_id=12,
              row_id="existing-row-uuid",
              title="New Document")
```

With initial content:
```
document_crud(method="create",
              table_id=5,
              field_id=12,
              title="New Document",
              data=[{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Hello world"}]}])
```

**row_id behavior:**
- Omit `row_id` → creates a new row in the table
- Provide `row_id` → adds document to an existing row (user must provide the row ID)

### Listing Documents

```
document_crud(method="list")
```

Returns all TipTap documents with their location (tableId, fieldId, rowId).

### Reading Documents

```
document_crud(method="read",
              document_id="uuid-string",
              table_id=5,
              field_id=12)
```

Returns full TipTap JSON content.

### Updating Documents

```
document_crud(method="update",
              document_id="uuid-string",
              table_id=5,
              field_id=12,
              data={"type": "doc", "content": [...]})
```

The `data` must be a complete TipTap document structure.

### TipTap JSON Format

```json
{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Plain text"}]},
    {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Title"}]},
    {"type": "bulletList", "content": [
      {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Item"}]}]}
    ]}
  ]
}
```

### Important Notes

- `table_id` and `field_id` are REQUIRED for create/read/update
- `row_id` is OPTIONAL for create: omit to create new row, provide to add to existing row
- Always `list` first to find document IDs (for read/update)
- Document IDs are UUID strings
- `data` for update must be complete TipTap JSON (not partial)
- Marks (bold, italic, etc.) go on text nodes: `{"type": "text", "text": "bold", "marks": [{"type": "bold"}]}`
